# Bushy Bodyguard with offspring {2} paid (four Moxen on turn 3): "create a 1/1 token copy of it" (CR 702.175a). The Bodyguard and its token
# copy each have the forage trigger. Bot1 has one Food (a Heaped Harvest cast on turn 1) and no graveyard to speak of, so only one forage can be
# paid: the token's trigger resolves first (it is the newer object) and is accepted (the Food sacrificed, +2 counters on the 1/1 token,
# a 3/3), and the Bodyguard's own trigger then finds no Food and asks nothing: it stays a 2/1, the Harvest is gone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Heaped Harvest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Bushy Bodyguard
Island
Mox Sapphire
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

